WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.936
[Wil] Bladesmiths,
welcome to the Forge.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.404
In every one
of these competitions,

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.741
we have four bladesmiths
walk through that door,

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.842
but oftentimes
there's the presence

00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:12.545
of a fifth, unnamed bladesmith.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.548
[dramatic music playing]

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.418
Big BLU.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.920
[Bryce]
<i> What on earth are we gonna do</i>

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.689
with this giant piece
of history right here?

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:26.292
[Wil]<i> This Big BLU power hammer
 has facilitated the success</i>

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.794
<i> of almost every single</i>
Forged in Fire<i> champion</i>

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.596
that's walked through
that door.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.999
On the other hand, it has
literally chewed up

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:36.169
<i> and spit out the dreams</i>

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:37.804
<i> of other bladesmiths...</i>

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.338
Oh man!

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.040
...turning
their forge experience

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:43.143
into an absolute nightmare.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.946
Well, now it's time to replace
and retire Big BLU.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.848
But not before we rip out
its beating heart

00:00:49.948 --> 00:00:51.751
and turn that high carbon piston

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.387
into four competition choppers

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.223
<i> that fall between 11 and 13
 inches in length.</i>

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.925
<i> Your blades at the end
 of this round</i>

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:01.494
<i> must not exceed
 22 inches overall.</i>

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.764
Good luck, bladesmiths.
Your time starts now.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.131
[Bryce]<i> We only have three hours</i>

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:07.733
to take the thing apart
and make a knife?

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.034
<i> That's insane.</i>

00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:10.236
[Colton]<i> We all decide</i>

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.171
we're gonna work
together to take this apart.

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.174
<i> It'll benefit all of us.</i>

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.643
It's really a testament to the
competitorship we have here...

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.012
We're coming. She's going.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:21.914
...when you watch these guys
help one another

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:24.717
disassemble that machine
very quickly.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.153
We know we're all working
off the same piece of steel.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.221
<i> There's no working
 against each other.</i>

00:01:29.254 --> 00:01:30.790
<i> We gotta get this thing off.</i>

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:32.959
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.960
[Bryce]<i> We all have
 an even amount of steel</i>

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.463
to make a knife
to meet parameters.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.533
That's about a one-
and-three-eighths-inch shaft.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.369
[Colton]<i> When the steel
finally gets up to temperature,</i>

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.771
I start squishing
the steel down.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:49.341
I'm pretty optimistic about how
fast I can get this to run out.

00:01:49.441 --> 00:01:52.578
I just purchased a press
about a week ago

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.080
<i> so I have a little bit
 of experience.</i>

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.516
But up until that point,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.719
I've basically just depended
on these guys right here.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:02.555
[Craig]<i> On the whole,
 my progress is doin' well.</i>

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:06.091
But I'm definitely the old guy
in the room.

00:02:06.191 --> 00:02:08.727
<i> It's me against
 three younger guys</i>

00:02:08.827 --> 00:02:11.330
that, uh, are probably a little
more physically fit than me.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.600
But maybe I'm a little more
mentally fit than them.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.234
[Wil] One hour has elapsed.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.570
You have two hours remaining
to finish your work.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.172
I realize after about
two passes through Big BLU

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.608
<i> I'm spending too much time
 on Big BLU itself.</i>

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.544
I'm not letting my metal
heat up as fast.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.914
<i> So time is ticking by because
 I'm not really moving metal.</i>

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:31.851
It looks like Bryce has some
maybe different thicknesses

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.052
on his blade.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.787
You can see there are
dark spots

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:37.856
and then there are spots that
are holding a little more heat.

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:40.526
[David] It's sitting under
the actual burner

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.696
and he's not moving that steel
back and forth, evening it out.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.099
[Colton]<i> After I get
 profiling done,</i>

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:48.801
I get ready to drill some holes

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.970
for the pins
in the next round.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.940
Colton is over here
using a punch

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.742
as he kinda marks some holes
for his tang.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.377
[David] That's smart work.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:01.414
I do this now because
in the next round,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.516
<i> it will be quenched and hard</i>

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:07.787
and sometimes you can't drill
holes in hardened steel.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.255
[Wil] The blades
are coming along.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.924
We should have some
beautiful competition choppers

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.726
in the next hour or so.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.097
Right now, I'm just gonna go
grind the handle a bit more,

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.966
tweak it,
uh, shorten it up,

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.734
and then we'll be good
to start quenching.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.336
<i> I'm thinking, "Wow.</i>

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:27.706
I have never used a grinder
like this before."

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.843
This shop compared to mine
blows mine outta the water.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:34.246
It feels a little odd
using other people's tools

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:36.749
but you just gotta roll
with the punches.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.386 line:0%
<i> Before I heat treat,</i>

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.388 line:0%
I definitely am thermocycling
that blade.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.824 line:0%
Now I gotta make sure there's
not gonna be any cracking

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.992
<i> or tinging or warps
 when I put it in that oil.</i>

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.128
Quenching!

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.764
-Quenching?
-Not bad. That was a good color.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.032
[David] Good job. Look at that.

00:03:54.132 --> 00:03:54.933
Looks pretty straight from here.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.969
[Bryce]<i> It looks amazing.</i>

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:58.638
I'm pumped right now. Let's go.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.443
[dramatic music playing]

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:09.182
[Wil] Over here, we got a quench
outta Colton.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.350
[Colton]<i> I'm feeling pretty good
 with this quench.</i>

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:16.455
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:18.691
Bladesmiths, shut down
your machines! Drop your tools!

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:21.560
This first round of competition
is over!

00:04:21.693 --> 00:04:24.563
Bladesmiths,
welcome to our strength test:

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.231
the bamboo chop.

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:27.733
This tough, springy material

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.735
is not only gonna test the edge
of your blades,

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.337
but it's gonna test the overall
construction of your knife.

00:04:32.437 --> 00:04:33.839
This is gonna be a lot of fun.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.973
At least for me.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.308
Colton, you're up first.

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:37.276
-How you feeling?
-Good.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.679
Good? I feel good too.
Let's go.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.613 line:0%
[dramatic music playing]

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:45.051 line:0%
[Colton]<i> I know J. hits
 really, really hard.</i>

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.919 line:0%
<i> So I'm a little nervous</i>

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.688 line:0%
<i> that the amount of force
 he's gonna put into that</i>

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:52.492
might make the blade just snap
in half when he hits the bamboo.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:54.560
[grunting]

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:57.697
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.472
[tense music playing]

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:09.008
Nice job, Colton.
Edge held up well.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:12.711
You fixed that little warp
so everything stayed lined up.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.881
The handle, would've liked to
have been beefed up a little.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:19.185
That's on the narrow side.
But overall, good job.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.920
Thank you.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.588
Hey, Bryce. How you doing?

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:24.323
-Doing good.
-Gonna make Big BLU proud?

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:25.991
-I am.
-[J.] Let's see.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:27.460 line:0%
[dramatic music playing]

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.329 line:0%
[Bryce]<i> Soon as J. grabs
 my blade, I was like, "Wow."</i>

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.531 line:0%
<i> I'm worried my blade's
 a little bit thin</i>

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.668 line:0%
so I'm hoping it doesn't crack
or splinter off.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.403
[grunting]

00:05:38.503 --> 00:05:40.940
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:05:48.046 --> 00:05:49.147
Nice work, Bryce.

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:52.284
It's not the prettiest knife
I've ever seen.

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:53.886
But your edge held up fine.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.388
Your handle, little bit long.

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:58.958
Kinda simple.
But overall, good job.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.225
Thank you.

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:01.593
And then there was Craig.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.396
-How you feeling, bud?
-Feeling good. Ready to go.

00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:05.831
All right. Let's see
how your knife feels.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.400 line:0%
-Let's do it.
-[dramatic music playing]

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.269 line:0%
[Craig]<i> As I watch
 the other tests going on,</i>

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:12.438 line:0%
<i> I'm just kinda getting
 more amped up.</i>

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.438 line:0%
<i> I'm ready for it.</i>

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:17.043 line:0%
But you cannot make
those butterflies settle down.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.947
[grunting]

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:23.383
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.390
[tense music playing]

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.525
-[J.] It survived!
-[laughs]

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:35.194
-[J.] Good job, Craig.
-Thank you.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.363
The edge is perfect.
Nothing wrong with it.

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:39.431
I like the look of it,
the feel of it.

00:06:39.564 --> 00:06:42.935
-Overall, did a very good job.
-Thank you.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.808
All right, bladesmiths.
This is our sharpness test:

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.143
the rope bridge slice.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.611
Unlike the strength test,

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.246
this is all about what the edge
of your weapon

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.848
will do to the rope.

00:06:56.348 --> 00:06:58.250
-Colton, you're first. Ready?
-Yep.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:59.551
Let's do this.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:02.021
[tense music playing]

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:17.470
Man. Good cutting.
Good cut.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.006
All right, Colton, let's talk
about your chopper here.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:23.075
Nice and clean lines.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:27.346
Shiny. And more importantly,
one and done for every slice.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:28.781
It will cut.

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:32.284
-Bryce, your turn. Ready?
-I'm ready.

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:33.385
Let's do this.

00:07:33.485 --> 00:07:35.721
[tense music playing]

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:47.533
-Yeah.
-Good job.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.134
Good job. Good job.

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.135
Well, Bryce...

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.972
I think that Bryce is right.
[laughs]

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.673
Your edge is sharp.

00:07:54.773 --> 00:07:56.775
Your handle construction here

00:07:56.876 --> 00:07:59.912
does tend to be a little bit
shallow right there

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:02.448
to where it allows my hand
to fall forward

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:04.449
and there's a little bit
big space right there.

00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:07.687
But most of all, sir...
it will cut.

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:08.687
Thank you.

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:10.923
-All right, old timer.
-[chuckles]

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:13.291
-You ready for this?
-Ready as I'm getting.

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:14.259
Let's do this.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.562
[Craig]<i> The first two blades go
 and they slice perfectly</i>

00:08:17.662 --> 00:08:19.899
<i> and all I'm expecting to see</i>

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:22.368
is my knife bounce
right off that rope.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.904
[tense music playing]

00:08:32.812 --> 00:08:34.013
[grumbles]

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:35.481
[laughs]

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:38.284
All right, Craig.
What is there not to like?

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.619
It's got a nice curved edge

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.389
to when you're swinging it,
I can feel the curve

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.224
and it slices nicely.

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:47.760
And most of all, sir...
it will cut.

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:49.529
Wow. Thank you very much.

00:08:50.295 --> 00:08:52.198
[tense music playing]

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:54.232
Bladesmiths,
in these deliberations

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:55.667
the judges have to consider

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:57.770
not just how your blades
performed in the tests

00:08:57.836 --> 00:08:59.805
but also feel, fit, and finish.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.440
They've made
their final decision.

00:09:01.907 --> 00:09:04.509
It's time for one of you smiths
to leave the Forge.

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:07.013
[tense music playing]

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:10.016
Bryce, your blade
did not make the cut.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.451
[Doug] Bryce, you did great.

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:15.421
But all the blades
performed equally.

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:17.189
It came down to your handle.

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:20.192
Your handle, in comparison, was
a little larger than the others.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:22.360
It was a good, better, best.

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:23.629
Yours was good,

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.264
but the others
were better and best.

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:27.132
For that reason,
we're sending you home.

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:28.466
I understand.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.904
Bryce, please surrender
your blade.

00:09:32.037 --> 00:09:34.307
[Bryce]<i> I do 100% agree
 with the judges.</i>

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:35.974
<i> I respect their opinions
 on my blade.</i>

00:09:36.474 --> 00:09:37.876
This was a great competition.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.879
<i> I'm not disappointed
 in myself.</i>

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.947
My blade held up
to all the tests.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.083
<i> I came here to prove
 that I can</i>

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.485
<i> compete with
 other bladesmiths out there.</i>

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.588
I definitely believe
I proved it.

